Read a KVO context as text, for one named observer class only.

A DIAGNOSTIC, AND A DELIBERATELY NARROW ONE. A context is an ARBITRARY pointer: AppKit own bindings
machinery passes things through here that are not objects, so a probe that messaged every context
would crash the very run it is measuring. CIDER_TRACE_KVO_CONTEXT holds a substring of an OBSERVER
CLASS NAME and nothing outside that class is touched, which keeps the probe to registrations
already known to carry objects.

It reads at REGISTRATION, where the context is still alive. Reading it at notification time is the
thing under investigation and would be a probe that crashes on exactly the bug it is looking for.

WHAT IT ESTABLISHED, and it is the whole of task #249. Every context CCSegmentedControl registers:

    __NSCFConstantString   len=5   value      the literal, in the image, immortal
    __NSCFString           len=6   value1     heap
    __NSCFString           len=6   value2     heap
    __NSCFString           len=6   value3     heap

Swift Publisher uses the literal for segment 0 and COMPUTES the rest, and every computed one is six
ASCII characters. On macOS a string that short is a TAGGED POINTER: no allocation, nothing to
deallocate, so registering it as a context without retaining it is harmless, which is why the
application does it. Here it is a real heap object, it is autoreleased, the pool drains, and the
context the application still holds becomes garbage. That is the crash, and the missing feature is
tagged pointer string CREATION, which vendor/src/corefoundation/CFString.c does not have at all.

Task #249.
--- a/src/NSKeyValueObserving.m
+++ b/src/NSKeyValueObserving.m
@@ -647,6 +647,23 @@
         fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_KVO %s observes %s of %s context=%p\n", object_getClassName(observer),
                 _CiderKVOText(keyPath) ?: "(nil)", object_getClassName(self), context);
 
+        /*
+         * AND WHAT THE CONTEXT SAYS, FOR ONE NAMED OBSERVER CLASS ONLY.
+         *
+         * A context is an ARBITRARY pointer. AppKit own bindings machinery passes things through
+         * here that are not objects at all, so messaging every context would crash the run that is
+         * trying to measure it. CIDER_TRACE_KVO_CONTEXT holds a substring of an observer class
+         * name and nothing else is touched, which keeps the probe to registrations already known
+         * to carry objects. It is read at REGISTRATION, where the context is still alive; reading
